 strategies.", "FLUOROSCOPIC EVALUATION:A diagnostic procedure used to assess oropharyngeal dysphagia, involving real-time imaging to evaluate swallowing mechanics.", "CANCER PATIENTS:Cancer patients are individuals diagnosed with cancer who are undergoing treatment and may require nutritional support to manage their health. These patients often face various complications related to their condition, including dysphagia, which can further complicate their nutritional needs. As subjects of various studies, cancer patients are also the focus of research aimed at understanding the relationship between nutrition and treatment outcomes. Overall, the care and support of cancer patients encompass a comprehensive approach to address their medical and nutritional challenges during their treatment journey.", "NEOPLASIAS GASTROINTESTINALES:NEOPLASIAS GASTROINTESTINALES, or gastrointestinal neoplasms, represent a major cause of cancer mortality globally. These neoplasms are a significant health concern, highlighting the importance of nutritional intervention and support in their management. Given their impact on cancer mortality, there is a critical need for nutritional evaluation to aid in the treatment and prevention of these conditions.", "MALNUTRICIÓN RELACIONADA CON EL CÁNCER:Malnutrition related to cancer refers to the nutritional deficiencies that occur in patients due to the disease and its treatment, impacting their overall health.", "GRUPO ERAS:El grupo ERAS (Enhanced Recovery After Surgery) proporciona recomendaciones para la recuperación de pacientes con tumores digestivos.", "NUTRICIONAL RISK SCREENING 2002:", "INMUNONUTRICIÓN:INMUNONUTRICIÓN refers to the study and application of nutrition that influences the immune response, particularly in patients requiring artificial nutritional support. This nutritional approach aims to enhance the immune function of patients, especially those undergoing major surgeries, including surgeries related to gastric cancer. Additionally, immunonutrition is utilized to mitigate the hypermetabolic response to surgery and to promote recovery in these patients. Overall, INMUNONUTRICIÓN plays a crucial role in improving health outcomes for individuals with compromised immune systems due to surgical interventions.", "COMPLICACIONES POSTOPERATORIAS:Las complicaciones postoperatorias son efectos adversos que pueden surgir después de la cirugía, y su incidencia es especialmente alta en pacientes con cáncer, como aquellos con cáncer de páncreas y otros cánceres gastrointestinales. Estas complicaciones pueden ser más frecuentes debido a factores como la malnutrición y la pérdida de masa muscular, que son comunes en este grupo de pacientes. Para mitigar estos problemas, se busca implementar un tratamiento nutricional adecuado, lo que puede ayudar a reducir la aparición de complicaciones postoperatorias en estos individuos vulnerables.", "ÍNDICE PRONÓSTICO NUTRICIONAL:El índice pronóstico nutricional es un indicador que se asocia con el pronóstico de los pacientes con cáncer gástrico, donde un índice bajo se relaciona con un pronóstico desfavorable.", "NUTRICIÓN PERIOPERATORIA:La nutrición perioperatoria se refiere a la administración de nutrientes antes y después de la cirugía para reducir complicaciones y mejorar la recuperación.", "GUÍAS DE LA ESPEN:Las Guías de la ESPEN son recomendaciones para la práctica clínica en nutrición, especialmente en pacientes con cáncer."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}